steps for installing java:
1.install the maven (dnf list , dnf module list)
2.when we install maven automatically java will also be installed ..so give me the version path we need to have for java
3.give the /etc/profile.d/java.sh --> export JAVA_HOME=path of the java version
4.source /etc/profile.d/java.sh
5.if echo $JAVA_HOME ----> you should see the java path
6.check for mvn version and java version
7.create the /app
8.create the system variable by using useradd --system --home /app --shell /sbin/nologin --comments "add comments" roboshop
9.using curl -o /tmp/roboshop.zip http://git.xtusiisis//roboshop.zip
10.go to /app
11.unzip /tmp/roboshop.zip
12.make sure we have the pom.xml and all the file extracted
13.now run mvn clean package ----> this will download the dependecies, compile it,run the tests, build success and jar is generated
14.target is the folder where the jar file will be stored and that path will be given in service file
15.copy the service file and make sure we are giving the connections of the backend file
16.systemctl daemon-reload   ---> reload the systemd
17.systemctl restart servicename
18.systemctl enable servicename
19.systemctl start servicename
20.check the health ( http://localhost:8080/health) ,telnet, netstat -lntp , ps -ef | grep service name  